&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job title:&lt;/strong&gt; Product Manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris — Hybrid - 3 days in office&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; €45,600 - €57,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Product Management - Customer Care Value Stream&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to: &lt;/strong&gt;Head of Product&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is based in France and requires the successful candidate to be based in or willing to relocate to France. Fluent French and English (spoken and written) are essential for this position.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please submit your profile in English.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today&#39;s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future. Leveraging Data, AI, and real-time decision-making we turn energy complexity into growth opportunities for our partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable and affordable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With teams across Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where in the world of Kaluza will I be working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be specifically working with the team building out our contact centre solution and the &lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Agent Experience (KAE).&lt;/strong&gt; Our Customer Care platform powers AI-driven, cost-efficient service operations for global energy retailers, enabling personalised customer experiences across contact centres, digital channels, and case management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is mission-critical to Kaluza’s vision. You will lead the product strategy, delivery, and client outcomes for Kaluza’s Customer Care solutions for&lt;strong&gt; ENGIE France&lt;/strong&gt;, while contributing to the evolution of our Global Core capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Customer Care Product Manager, you are accountable for the outcomes delivered by your product. You will ensure design and engineering teams have absolute clarity on priorities and scope to drive meaningful results for end users and commercial value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Product Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the Customer Care product strategy and roadmap for Kaluza clients in France, balancing Global Core reuse with specific French localisation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build High-Value Solutions: &lt;/strong&gt;Develop our suite of tools for the Contact Centre Solution, including CCaaS (Contact Centre as a Service) and Case Management, to enable efficient, high-value conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive AI Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Utilise the latest AI technology to automate and personalise the customer experience and champion agent productivity tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foster Client Partnerships:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Act as the senior product counterpart to client stakeholders (such as ENGIE), leading workshops and translating their needs into scalable capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Execute &amp;amp; Optimise:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Lead cross-functional teams (engineering, design, data, and commercial) to ensure efficient delivery, removing blockers and resolving cross-team dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Operational Excellence:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Define and track key contact centre metrics such as AHT, FCR, CSAT, and NPS to ensure solutions deliver measurable cost-to-serve improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Is this the job for me?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are the right person for us if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have significant &lt;strong&gt;product leadership experience in enterprise SaaS &lt;/strong&gt;and have worked in agile product organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess deep knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;contact centre operations &lt;/strong&gt;and agent workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working with&lt;strong&gt; French enterprise clients&lt;/strong&gt; and a strong understanding of localisation requirements, including language and regulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are skilled at &lt;strong&gt;stakeholder management at the executive level&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to manage trade-offs between speed and long-term value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are data-oriented, with an adeptness for using &lt;strong&gt;operational metrics&lt;/strong&gt; to assess product performance and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a background in &lt;strong&gt;energy retail or utilities &lt;/strong&gt;(this will set you apart!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited by &lt;strong&gt;AI-driven automation&lt;/strong&gt;, including voice bots and agent assist technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you&#39;re excited about joining us and think you have some of what we&#39;re looking for, even if you&#39;re not 100% sure, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about working at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://kaluza.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=http://kaluza.com&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1772730023496000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw2WQ4QggVd_VKIz_hhKv_E_&quot;&gt;Kaluza&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;on our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1772730023496000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw0ieu808CO6v15ojfSZWHzP&quot;&gt;careers page&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1772730023496000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1r5cAEyzI_Xc26WGuLbLZx&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You can also find our Applicant Data Protection Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.kaluza.com/applicant-data-protection-notice&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest. Our mission to deliver honest financial products that improve lives extends beyond borders. Consumers across the globe need safe, transparent financing. Our retail partners need Affirm to be there for them, wherever that might be. To help achieve this vision, we are expanding our product lines and becoming a global company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The International Consumer product team is responsible for building and scaling Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products and experiences across international markets. This includes our apps, wallets, marketplace, and related offerings that help consumers discover, use, and manage Affirm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager on the International Consumer team, you will drive the strategy, execution, and growth of Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products across international markets – from iterating on the product vision, refining the product strategy, developing a roadmap, and leading execution.&lt;br&gt;In this role, you will work closely with a broad set of cross functional teams across the entire business, as well as a number of engineering teams. Effective stakeholder management and ability to successfully navigate organizational dynamics are a must for success. You should be commercially minded, be high agency with a bias towards action, and comfortable having technical conversations (and opinions).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive the execution, growth, and scale of Affirm’s consumer products and experiences across international markets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products and adapt them for international markets by understanding consumer needs, analyzing performance data, and iterating on the product’s features and capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive success metrics by shipping high impact work that meaningfully moves the needle for Affirm’s business and customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner effectively with engineering teams across the organization to drive product development and prioritization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders (such as Design, Research, Analytics, Marketing, Legal, Compliance, Credit, Fraud, etc.) to shape your product roadmap and incorporate legal, governance, and regulatory oversight into your products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand Affirm’s international consumers at a deep level: what’s important to them, what drives their decision making, why they love Affirm, and what they wish we could do better&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify and create the experiences that make it seamless for consumers to discover, use, and manage Affirm across our apps, wallets, marketplace, and related direct-to-consumer offerings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn’t your first rodeo. You’ve directly managed technical software products from kick-off to post-launch – driving meaningful business impact that you can speak to&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have experience working on consumer technology products in Canada, UK, EU, or Australia (bonus points if that experience is in fintech, commerce, marketplaces, or payments)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re equally comfortable diving into technical details with an engineer, iterating on a Figma with a designer, and breaking down a funnel with a data analyst&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have the discipline, organizational skills, and interpersonal communication skills necessary to navigate complex organizational dynamics – you have specific examples of times when you’ve secured a decision from a broad group of senior stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve worked in an environment where you were reliant on engineering teams outside of your direct purview and were able to effectively influence them to prioritize and build what you needed for your product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re the kind of person who cares about getting things done. You have a bias towards action and can effectively navigate obstacles and blockers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can turn incomplete, conflicting, or ambiguous inputs into a solid action plan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have direct experience shipping high-quality products on time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You feel comfortable jumping into the commercial aspects of product development – you’re able to connect customer needs, product decisions, and business outcomes, and make clear tradeoffs across them&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Grade - N&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grade - 5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents). In addition, the employees may be eligible for equity rewards offered by Affirm Holdings, Inc. (parent company).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;GBR base pay range per year: &amp;nbsp;£120,000–£168,000 GBP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location - Remote UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – E-Commerce Web Upper Funnel [Permanent - CDI] (f/m/d)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Paris or Lille, France&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Decathlon E-Commerce Web – Scope Upper Funnel&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of Decathlon’s global digital ecosystem, our &lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Web&lt;/strong&gt; team builds the online destination for millions of sports lovers worldwide. The &lt;strong&gt;Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt; scope is the front door of our digital experience: from landing on the homepage and navigating categories, to discovering products via search, AI-driven recommendations, conversational shopping, retail media placements, and inspiring content. Our mission is to seamlessly guide users from inspiration to intent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining this high-traffic Web Product organization means operating at massive scale where speed, discovery excellence, SEO, targeted monetization, and next-gen personalized user journeys drive our everyday business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Staff Product Manager – Upper Funnel&lt;/strong&gt;, you will provide the strategic direction, functional architecture, and product leadership needed to scale and modernize the discovery and exploration experience across Decathlon&#39;s web platform. Operating with high autonomy, you will address complex challenges across search performance, catalog structuring, retail media integration, and emerging AI paradigm shifts like conversational interface models and agentic workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission centers on 4 strategic pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Strategic Alignment, Stakeholder Management &amp;amp; Upper Funnel Vision&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Holistic Discovery &amp;amp; Engagement Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;: Define and drive the strategic vision for upper funnel web touchpoints (Homepage, Category/Listing Pages, Search Engine, Navigation Taxonomy, Retail Media Ad Placements, Conversational Assistants, and Inspiration Hubs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;: Partner with global business directors, commercial/merchandising leads, SEO specialists, retail media monetization teams, and AI platform engineering leads to align executive leadership around major web platform shifts and discovery roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Macro Metrics &amp;amp; Funnel Performance&lt;/strong&gt;: Track, measure, and optimize key upper funnel metrics across the customer journey: Organic/Direct Traffic, Search CTR, Category Depth, Conversational Engagement &amp;amp; Intent Resolution Rate, Ad Yield/eCPM, Bounce Rate, Product Detail Page (PDP) Click-through Rate, and Top-of-Funnel Conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Functional Architecture &amp;amp; Web Ecosystem Orchestration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Functional Architect&lt;/strong&gt;: Define boundary maps and functional scope across web squads (Search &amp;amp; Conversational Discovery, Taxonomy &amp;amp; Merchandising, Personalization/Recommendations, Retail Media &amp;amp; Sponsored Listings) to eliminate overlap and friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tight Triad Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: Work in close sync with Staff/Principal Web Engineers and Staff UX/UI Designers to align frontend performance (Core Web Vitals), modular web design systems, micro-frontend architecture, conversational UI patterns, and backend search/ad-serving APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seamless Omnichannel &amp;amp; Funnel Handoff&lt;/strong&gt;: Ensure fluid transitions from external acquisition channels into the web upper funnel, balancing organic product discovery and agentic assistance with sponsored/retail media inventory while designing seamless handoffs toward the lower funnel (PDP, Cart &amp;amp; Checkout).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Strategic Sparring &amp;amp; Product De-Risking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trusted Strategic Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;: Serve as a sparring partner for Group Product Managers (GPMs) and Product Managers (PMs) within the Web &amp;amp; E-Commerce domain, helping them navigate complex search algorithms, LLM agent architectures, ad server integrations, taxonomy dependencies, and high-volume web constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;De-Risking High-Stakes Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;: Formulate and execute validation strategies for high-risk discovery and monetization concepts (e.g., visual/voice search, conversational product advisors, agentic auto-replenishment/bundles, sponsored product placements).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Experimentation at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;: Design and lead high-volume A/B and multivariate testing strategies, balancing conversational interaction models and ad impression density against organic conversion performance using CRO frameworks and Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Elevating Product Craft &amp;amp; Modern Web Capabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-First, Agentic &amp;amp; Monetization Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: Champion the organizational adoption of cloud-native AI platforms (e.g., Google Vertex AI), conversational frameworks, agentic e-commerce patterns, and modern retail media capabilities to amplify both user experience and platform revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web Craft &amp;amp; Best Practices&lt;/strong&gt;: Upskill the PM community in modern web product practices, continuous discovery frameworks, technical web performance optimization, and data-informed decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community Multiplier&lt;/strong&gt;: Elevate the overall bar of the Product Management organization as a thought leader without acting as a direct line manager.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING TO THE TABLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;E-Commerce Web Scale (7+ years)&lt;/strong&gt;: Proven track record in Product Management with hands-on experience scaling high-traffic e-commerce web platforms (Upper Funnel, Search, Merchandising, or Navigation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Upper Funnel &amp;amp; SEO Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Deep understanding of top-of-funnel mechanics, technical SEO, site search algorithms, taxonomy design, and conversion rate optimization (CRO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data &amp;amp; Discovery Mastery&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong expertise in web analytics (GA4/Amplitude/Contentsquare), high-traffic A/B testing frameworks, quantitative/qualitative user research, and Opportunity Solution Trees (OST).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Functional Architecture &amp;amp; Scoping&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to decompose complex e-commerce catalog, ad-tech, and AI/search problems into modular MVP/V0/V1 execution strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Storytelling &amp;amp; Alignment&lt;/strong&gt;: Exceptional ability to translate complex search/agentic architectures, retail media revenue drivers, UX metrics, and conversion data into compelling narratives for executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Pluses &amp;amp; Emerging Tech Strengths&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Google Vertex AI&lt;/strong&gt;: Practical experience using Google Vertex AI (for Search, Recommendations, or custom ML/LLM model deployment) is a major plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversational &amp;amp; Agentic E-Commerce&lt;/strong&gt;: Solid understanding or experience with conversational AI interfaces (chat/voice product advisors) and agentic commerce concepts (autonomous intent-matching, task-oriented AI agents) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retail Media &amp;amp; Monetization&lt;/strong&gt;: Experience with Retail Media concepts and ad management (sponsored products, ad-server integrations, balancing yield vs. UX) is a major plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soft Skills &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong strategic influence, ability to thrive in ambiguity, passion for cross-functional collaboration in Triad, and an empathetic approach to mentoring junior PMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid Work Model&lt;/strong&gt; (Paris or Lille base) 2 days of remote work per week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tailored Equipment&lt;/strong&gt; (Mac or Windows, according to mission and sustainability commitments);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Exposure&lt;/strong&gt;: Local project team within a global retail and digital network with international career opportunities;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: Internal/external trainings, skill development programs, and conference attendance;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;: Competitive salary package including employee stock ownership, profit-sharing, and monthly/quarterly performance bonuses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL CONTEXT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if technology allowed us to push the boundaries and take sports experiences to new levels? That&#39;s exactly our goal at Decathlon Digital! We are a team of 5,000+ experts in software engineering, product management, data, cloud, and cybersecurity, distributed across Paris, Lille, and Amsterdam. Together, we are creating the largest digital sports platform, leveraging tech innovation from design to value chain optimization, connected experiences and product second life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changing the game for good&lt;/strong&gt;. We are in this for the love of sports. And like everything we love, we want it to last. That’s why we are embarking on a journey to create a more sustainable tech model, reducing our direct environmental impact while maintaining a safe, diverse, and inclusive space for all our people to learn and thrive together. Team up with us to design the digital future of sports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Manager – Innovation &amp;amp; Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Location: Paris (Hybrid) | Practice Area: Technology &amp;amp; Engineering | Type: Permanent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Imaginez et construisez des produits qui répondent aux vrais besoins des utilisateurs et transforment durablement les services financiers.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco recherche des &lt;strong&gt;Product Managers&lt;/strong&gt; pour accompagner les acteurs majeurs des services financiers et de l&#39;énergie dans la conception de produits utiles à leurs clients et créateurs de valeur pour leur organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au sein de notre capability &lt;strong&gt;Tech, Product &amp;amp; Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, vous intégrerez des équipes pluridisciplinaires réunissant Product Managers, ingénieurs, développeurs et experts métiers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Votre rôle sera de comprendre les besoins des utilisateurs, identifier les bonnes problématiques à résoudre et transformer ces insights en produits simples, viables et performants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Vous intégrerez également de manière pragmatique les outils d’IA et d’automatisation approuvés dans vos méthodes de travail pour accélérer la recherche, l’analyse et l’expérimentation, tout en conservant le jugement humain au cœur des décisions produit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vos responsabilités&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travailler avec des équipes produit pluridisciplinaires pour identifier les problématiques utilisateurs prioritaires et concevoir des solutions à la fois désirables, viables et techniquement réalisables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intervenir sur l’ensemble du cycle de vie produit, de la discovery et de la recherche utilisateur jusqu’au lancement, à la mesure de la performance et à l’optimisation continue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combiner études de marché, recherche qualitative, données quantitatives et comportements observés pour construire une compréhension structurée des utilisateurs&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;et exploiter, lorsque pertinent, des outils d’IA approuvés pour accélérer l’analyse et faire émerger des insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intégrer les contraintes propres aux services financiers – réglementation, risques et contrôles, protection des données et viabilité économique – dans les décisions produit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter le produit par les résultats et la valeur créée pour les utilisateurs et le business, en testant différentes approches plutôt qu’en vous concentrant uniquement sur la production de livrables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compétences et expériences désirées&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Au moins 5 ans d’expérience en Product Management, acquise au sein d’une entreprise technologique ou d’un cabinet de conseil.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience avérée dans la discovery, la conception et le développement de produits de bout en bout, idéalement sur des expériences web et mobiles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne maîtrise des méthodologies produit – Jobs-to-be-Done, personas, frameworks de priorisation, KANO, Lean Startup – et des méthodes de delivery Agile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une capacité démontrée à collaborer avec des designers, ingénieurs/développeurs, équipes métiers et parties prenantes, ainsi qu’à traiter des problématiques complexes à partir de données et d&#39;insights structurés.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne connaissance de la banque et des services financiers, associée à une curiosité pour les usages de l’IA et des workflows AI-enabled permettant d&#39;améliorer la qualité, la rapidité ou la pertinence du travail produit, dans un cadre responsable et avec validation humaine.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vous êtes à l’aise pour travailler en français et en anglais dans des environnements internationaux.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi rejoindre Capco?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capco est un cabinet de conseil international, spécialisé dans les services financiers.&lt;br&gt;Fondé en 1998, le cabinet compte aujourd’hui plus de 7 000 collaborateurs dans 36 bureaux à travers le monde, dont 160 à Paris.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Challenger reconnu face aux grands noms du conseil, Capco se distingue par sa double expertise métier et technologique, au service de la stratégie comme de l’exécution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notre promesse : accompagner la transformation de nos clients dans un monde en constante mutation – réglementaire, technologique et opérationnel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous intervenons à l’intersection du business, de la réglementation et de la tech, en mobilisant des équipes pluridisciplinaires, expérimentées et engagées.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nos marqueurs distinctifs :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une spécialisation sectorielle forte&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nous apportons à nos clients une compréhension approfondie de leurs enjeux métiers, en particulier dans la banque, les marchés de capitaux et l’énergie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une approche collaborative et sur mesure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nous intégrons les équipes clients, adaptons nos méthodes à leur culture et co-construisons des solutions concrètes et opérationnelles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L’excellence comme exigence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Notre ambition est d’obtenir des résultats mesurables et durables pour nos clients – et de toujours viser la valeur ajoutée.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Un esprit “One Capco”&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nos équipes collaborent à l’échelle internationale pour mobiliser les meilleures expertises et partager les bonnes pratiques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Une culture entrepreneuriale et inclusive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;L’innovation, l’initiative et le mérite sont au cœur de notre modèle. Nous valorisons les idées, la diversité et le progrès collectif.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nos expertises s’articulent autour de 6 métiers complémentaires&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stratégie &amp;amp; Transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance, Risque &amp;amp; Conformité&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product, Innovation &amp;amp; Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conseil Tech (Advisory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering (Delivery)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Chez Capco, nous vous offrons&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un environnement de travail international centré sur l’innovation et la création de valeur pour nos clients bancaires et assuranciels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un parcours de formation continu adapté à vos besoins, pour acquérir de nouvelles compétences et développer une réelle expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une organisation de travail hybride (charte télétravail de 2 jours par semaine)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une rémunération compétitive avec un bonus lié à la performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Un PEE avec un abondement de 2903€ par an&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une culture d’entreprise entrepreneuriale, inclusive et méritocratique, de nouveau certifiée Great Place To Work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des initiatives pour construire le Capco de demain&amp;nbsp;:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;#BeYourselfAtWork&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Woman@capco&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RSE (forfait mobilité durable, jour de solidarité, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Des communautés métiers, sportives et culturelles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Capco Paris, handicap visible ou invisible, parcours atypique ou classique, toutes les candidatures sont les bienvenues et seront traitées avec équité.&lt;/p&gt;
