&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Energy Exemplar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In an era where the world is rapidly advancing towards a cleaner future through decarbonization, Energy Exemplar’s mission lies in ‘Empowering Transformative Energy Decisions’. Founded in 1999 in Adelaide, Australia, our award-winning software portfolio encompassing the modeling and simulation platform PLEXOS®, Aurora, and Adapt2, is trusted by innovative organizations across the globe. Through our technology and people, we strive to enable stakeholders from across the entire energy value chain to revolutionize the energy ecosystem and to collaboratively plan and execute for a sustainable energy future with unprecedented clarity, speed, and innovation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our impact is global and is being recognized across the industry. Some of our recent accolades include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;SaaS Company of the Year (2025) – Global Business Tech Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Environmental Impact Award (2025) – E+E Leaders Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;IPPAI (Independent Power Producers Association of India) Power Awards (2025) - Winners&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Finalist: Platts Global Energy Awards (2024) – Grid Edge category&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Finalist: Reuters Global Energy Transition Awards (2024) – Technologies of Change&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Top 50 Marketing Team (2024) – Voted by the public at the ICON Awards.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How We Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Energy Exemplar is growing fast around 30% year on year and, that growth is driven by how we work. We trust our team to deliver great results from wherever they work best, whether that’s at home, in the office, or on the move.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a global team that values ownership, integrity, and innovation. You’ll be supported to balance work and life in a way that works for you, and empowered to take initiative, solve problems, and make an impact, regardless of your background, location, or role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our four core values, Customer Success, One Global Team, Integrity &amp;amp; Ownership, and Innovation Excellence aren’t just words. They show up in how we collaborate, how we solve, and how we grow together.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Energy Market Analyst – Trading, you will sit within Energy Exemplar’s EMEA Solutions team, acting as a key technical partner to power trading customers across the region. You will combine deep knowledge of electricity markets and fundamental energy market modelling with an understanding of trading desk workflows to help customers use PLEXOS to support commercial and trading decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will work closely with power trading organisations, the EMEA Sales team, Solutions colleagues and Product teams. You will support customers across the full lifecycle from pre-sales demonstrations and proof-of-concept engagements through to model implementation, onboarding, optimisation and ongoing customer success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be accountable for delivering high quality modelling solutions that address customer needs, translating complex market and modelling concepts into actionable insights, and identifying opportunities to improve how trading organisations use fundamental modelling in their decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly collaborative and customer facing role, with the opportunity to work with leading organisations across EMEA, contribute to thought leadership in power trading, and influence the continued development of PLEXOS for trading applications. The role can be based from Energy Exemplar’s London office or remotely within Europe, with international travel across EMEA as required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Primary Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted technical advisor to power trading customers, developing strong relationships and understanding their commercial objectives, workflows and modelling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development and delivery of fundamental energy market modelling solutions using PLEXOS and related technologies to support trading and portfolio decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers to analyse modelling outputs, validate assumptions and data, and continuously improve models to ensure they provide relevant and actionable market insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the full customer lifecycle, including requirements gathering, onboarding, training, troubleshooting, model optimisation and ongoing technical support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the EMEA Sales team on prospective customer engagements, including technical demonstrations, proof-of-concept studies, presentations and responses to detailed functional and technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use scripting, automation, APIs, CLI tools and cloud-based environments to develop efficient modelling workflows and integrate PLEXOS into customer processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Solutions teams to communicate customer needs, identify opportunities for product improvement and contribute to the development of trading-focused capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct market research and develop original analysis on emerging trends in power markets and trading, contributing to thought leadership, webinars, conferences and customer-facing content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple customer engagements and priorities across EMEA, balancing delivery, stakeholder management and commercial requirements in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel internationally across the EMEA region when required to support customers, sales opportunities, training and industry engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Candidate Requirements &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in energy markets, with a strong understanding of electricity market fundamentals, energy economics, power system operations and/or energy trading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience using fundamental energy market supply and demand models, including optimisation, unit commitment or dispatch modelling, to analyse electricity markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of power trading and electricity market dynamics, including how modelling can support price forecasting, market analysis, portfolio decisions, risk assessment and trading strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python or similar scripting skills, with experience using code to automate analytical or modelling workflows and work with data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to interpret complex modelling outputs, challenge assumptions and translate analysis into clear commercial insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build credibility and rapport with both technical and commercial audiences, including traders and other senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, customer requirements and competing priorities in a fast-paced, customer-facing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A tertiary qualification in Electrical Engineering, Energy Economics, Operations Research, or a related discipline, ideally with a focus on electricity systems or energy markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired but not required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hands on experience with&amp;nbsp;PLEXOS or another commercial energy market optimisation platform such as EPSI, BID3, Antares, SDDP or PROMOD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience working within or closely with a power trading desk, including exposure to day-ahead, intraday, balancing or other electricity markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying fundamental modelling to cross-border flows, congestion analysis, ancillary services, capacity markets, portfolio optimisation, VaR or hedging strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with APIs, CLI tools and cloud-based computation environments, particularly where these have been used to integrate energy market models into automated trading or analytical workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Energy Exemplar is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all team members. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, experiences, identities, and abilities. Please let us know if you require accommodations at any stage of the recruitment process—we&#39;re here to support you in showcasing your full potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Energy Exemplar respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal data you share during the recruitment process. This Candidate &lt;a&gt;Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; explains how we collect, use, and protect your personal information when you apply for a role with us.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🧡&lt;strong&gt; About Alma&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;At Alma, we believe sustainable commerce depends on fair, well‑balanced trade. Because finance plays a pivotal role in business, our mission is to put it back in its rightful place - serving merchants and consumers. Our installment and deferred payment solutions help merchants boost sales by 20% or more, increase customer loyalty, and deliver a seamless shopping experience - without encouraging bad debt. As the buy now pay later leader in France and active in 10 European countries, we&#39;ve empowered over +25,000 merchants and 10 million consumers. With 400+ Almakers and €100M+ ARR, Alma is scaling rapidly across Europe as a member of the Next40, and we&#39;re just getting started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;👐&lt;strong&gt; About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Alma Wallet builds the payment experience of the Alma app. With the Alma card, consumers can pay with Alma anywhere, not only at our partner merchants. In the app, they manage their payments with the method of their choice: Apple Pay, Google Pay or local payment methods. By taking Alma beyond our merchant network, the Alma card is one of the company&#39;s key strategic bets. You will report to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/tony-miksa/&quot;&gt;Tony&lt;/a&gt;, Senior Engineering Manager, and work closely with Justine, Product Manager, to bring it to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This position is a CDI based in Paris, with a hybrid work model.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;💼&lt;strong&gt; About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver the Alma Wallet roadmap: &lt;/strong&gt;the Alma card, and bringing new payment methods (Apple Pay, Google Pay, local payment methods), identity verification and Open Banking to the mobile app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and grow the Alma Wallet squad&lt;/strong&gt; by supporting engineers’ development, hiring the right profiles and creating an environment where the team can do its best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build an effective delivery system&lt;/strong&gt; by improving team processes, rituals and collaboration with Product, Design and the other Consumer squads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver a strategic payment roadmap&lt;/strong&gt; covering the Alma card, Apple Pay and Google Pay, local payment methods, the consumer point-of-sale experience, identity verification and Open Banking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the technical bar and protect reliability&lt;/strong&gt; through code reviews, technical design discussions and a strong focus on the quality and resilience of payment flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🧰&lt;strong&gt; You will work with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mobile&lt;/em&gt;: Expo / EAS, React Native, TypeScript, TanStack Query, Redux Toolkit, Zod, Reanimated, Jest, Detox. Payment SDKs: Adyen, Stripe, &lt;a href=&quot;http://Checkout.com&quot;&gt;Checkout.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Back-end&lt;/em&gt;: Python, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, PostgreSQL, Redis, Pub/Sub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Infra &amp;amp; observability&lt;/em&gt;: GCP, Kubernetes, Docker, ArgoCD, Datadog, Sentry, OpenFeature.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tools&lt;/em&gt;: GitHub, Linear, Notion, Figma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🧩&lt;strong&gt; About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To succeed in this job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;You have 3+ years of experience managing or leading engineers, including hiring and supporting team development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;You have strong hands-on technical credibility in mobile or back-end engineering, and are comfortable reviewing code and leading architecture discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;You have experience delivering products in a cross-functional squad with Product and Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;You are fluent in both French and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;And it will be nice if you also&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Have experience in fintech or another regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Have worked with payment methods, payment service providers or PSP SDK integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Have contributed to a consumer mobile application used at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Have mobile engineering experience, ideally with React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Don&#39;t meet every single requirement? At Alma, we believe great hires come from diverse paths. If this role excites you, we encourage you to apply. We value potential, curiosity and the ability to grow as much as experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🧘&lt;strong&gt; What&#39;s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;If you join, you will be able to grow and impact on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the Alma Wallet squad from the ground up&lt;/strong&gt;, helping define its ways of working, team culture and engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own projects at the heart of Alma’s strategy&lt;/strong&gt;, including the Alma card, Apple Pay and Google Pay, local payment methods and the evolution of the consumer payment experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work on a modern, end-to-end product stack&lt;/strong&gt;, from Expo, React Native, React 19 and TypeScript 7 on mobile to Python and FastAPI on the back-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🤑&lt;strong&gt; Compensation &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Competitive salary based on 12 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Profit-sharing and employee savings plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Health insurance: 100% covered by Alma including family package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Disability insurance: 100% covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Sport: partnerships with Gymlib and Classpass, or €30/month reimbursement for your sports activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Maternity/paternity leave: salary maintained at 100% during leave with no seniority requirement. Return to work at 4/5 schedule paid at 100% for 8 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Sustainable Mobility Package (FMD): €544.80/year (excluding full-remote contracts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Meal vouchers: €10/day, 50% covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Mental health: free access to MindDay platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Paid time off: 25 days/year (+ additional paid leave granted for employees on executive contracts)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;Access to our Learning &amp;amp; Development Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;2 weeks of full remote possible per year in summer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🎯&lt;strong&gt; Interview Process&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video screen with Sara, Talent Acquisition Manager&lt;/strong&gt; — 30–45 minutes to discuss your experience, motivation and the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience interview with Tony Miksa, Hiring Manager&lt;/strong&gt; — 45 minutes to explore your management experience, technical background and fit with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coding test with a Software Engineering interviewer&lt;/strong&gt; — 45–90 minutes, depending on your main programming language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;System design interview with a Staff Engineer interviewer&lt;/strong&gt; — 60 minutes to discuss architecture, technical trade-offs and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coffee chat with members of the Consumer tribe&lt;/strong&gt; — 60 minutes with a combination of Product and Engineering team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li2&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reference checks&lt;/strong&gt; — two professional references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;🌍&lt;strong&gt; Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Alma, we believe that diversity fuels innovation and makes our community stronger. We are committed to building a workplace where every person feels seen, respected, and empowered to do their best work whatever their gender, background, ethnicity, age, sexual orientation, religion, disability or lived experience. As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome applicants from all walks of life, and all employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit, and business needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-113912706363268805m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coreweave.com&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re proud to be a Living Wage accredited Employer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Data Centre Design and Construction team is responsible for leading the expansion of CoreWeave&#39;s global footprint, managing the full lifecycle of mission-critical facility builds from pre-construction planning through commissioning and turnover. This team ensures our data centres are delivered on time, within budget, and to the highest standards of quality, safety, and operational excellence to support our high-performance cloud infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Data Center Construction Project Manager, you will serve as the primary owner&#39;s representative, leading the overall direction, completion, and financial outcomes of multiple data centre construction projects. In this full-time on-site role, you will administer contracts with developers and general contractors, maintaining rigorous oversight of drawings, specifications, change management, and statutory planning approvals. Your primary focus will involve supervising the installation, coordination, commissioning, and quality assurance of complex Mechanical, Electrical, and Plumbing (MEP) systems, power distribution, and cooling infrastructure. Additionally, you will drive project schedules, manage multi-million pound budgets, and partner cross-functionally with supply chain, design, and executive stakeholders to ensure seamless project turnover.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of construction project management experience with direct leadership on data centre construction projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical expertise in mission-critical infrastructure, with an emphasis on MEP systems, power distribution, cooling, and redundancy protocols.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing construction contracts, financial forecasting, budget development, change management, and cost estimation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of on-site project leadership, coordinating general contractors, subcontractors, statutory bodies, and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of pre-construction services, risk management, scheduling tools, and web-based project management software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on-site full-time and possess a valid driver&#39;s licence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Construction Management, Architecture, Engineering, or a related technical discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale mission-critical infrastructure projects with contract values exceeding £80M ($100M+).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized industry certifications, such as Project Management Professional (PMP) or LEED certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you&#39;re a good fit?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in investing in our people and value candidates who bring diversified experiences to our teams—even if you do not match 100% of the listed criteria.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You love to:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage the full lifecycle of complex technical projects and drive on-site construction execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re curious about:&lt;/strong&gt; The intricacies of data centre infrastructure, next-generation MEP systems, and scaling critical facility operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re an expert in:&lt;/strong&gt; Construction contract management, financial forecasting, and managing general contractors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast! We are in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We are not afraid of a little chaos, and we are constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for take-off, the organisation&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
