&lt;h2&gt;About us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/&quot;&gt;Constructor Labs&lt;/a&gt; is the research arm of Constructor Knowledge, based at Campus Ring 1 in Bremen, Germany. Our work is organized around three units: Knowledge Labs, Cyber Labs and Science Labs. We apply computing, software and robotics research to make scientists, teachers and students more effective, working with institutional partners that include CERN, NUS, Carnegie Mellon and Fraunhofer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://constructorlabs.org/solutions/edtech/&quot;&gt;EdTech practice&lt;/a&gt; produces research that runs in production. AI-supported remote proctoring is in use at the Irish Aviation Authority, Princess Nourah University and Saudi Electronic University, and our course delivery platform is used by CERN, EPFL, MariaDB and Acronis. For industry clients, we build tailored BSc, MSc and PhD pipelines, L&amp;amp;D operating models, AI upskilling programmes and customer training systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Constructor Labs Solutions (CLS)&lt;/strong&gt; is our client-facing systems integrator for the education and research sector, launching in September 2026. It brings audit and consultancy, content, platform, talent and R&amp;amp;D services together under a single contract, an offer few providers make to education buyers today. Delivery is orchestrated across several Constructor organizations: CUB, Nexford, Nexademy, EBAC, Constructor Labs and Constructor Tech. Our aim is to become the go-to systems integrator for education in EMEA by 2029.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will open EMEA markets for Constructor Labs Solutions as a quota-carrying individual contributor. The role rests on an established network among universities, online education providers, EdTech vendors and corporate L&amp;amp;D and research buyers, and on your ability to convert that network into signed engagements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with the marketing and delivery teams to build pipeline, establish the CLS brand and develop a case-study library. Supporting you are a credible research institution, named production references, an existing Constructor and Constructor Tech client base, and delivery capability across five service lines that can be combined into a single proposal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The sales motion is consultative. Engagements typically open with a low-risk paid diagnostic (Technology Landscape Assessment, Curriculum Gap Analysis or Learning Strategy Advisory), which you then convert into a multi-line implementation or managed-service mandate. Initial engagements start at around €150–250K in lifetime value and grow from there. Sales cycles in public higher education run six to twelve months, so you will manage a long-cycle institutional funnel alongside faster corporate L&amp;amp;D deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Reporting and scope&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Director of Sales &amp;amp; Marketing, Constructor Labs Solutions (shared with the Constructor Labs GM during Phase 1).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level:&lt;/strong&gt; Director, individual contributor. You will join an established sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory:&lt;/strong&gt; EMEA, with initial focus on DACH (Germany, Austria, Switzerland) and the UK and Ireland. Named accounts agreed quarterly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Segments:&lt;/strong&gt; traditional and online universities, EdTech providers and platform vendors, corporate L&amp;amp;D and corporate academies, research-intensive organizations, and publicly funded research programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Portfolio:&lt;/strong&gt; all five CLS service lines, namely Audit &amp;amp; Consultancy, Content, Platform, Talent and R&amp;amp;D Services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day-to-day, you will work with the Audit &amp;amp; Consultancy Practice Head on scoping, with Nexademy on content propositions, with Constructor Tech on platform architecture, and with the Labs&#39; principal investigators, who join client conversations to provide subject-matter credibility. Knowing which expert belongs in which conversation is central to the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline generation.&lt;/strong&gt; Around 70% of your time is spent on outbound activity: your own network, conference presence, sector associations, procurement frameworks and targeted account campaigns, supported by marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reference accounts.&lt;/strong&gt; Sign the first reference clients in EMEA and develop each one into a published case study, an active sponsor and a source of introductions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discovery and scoping.&lt;/strong&gt; Map the client&#39;s learning or research operating model and quantify the problem in their own measures: cost per course, time to accreditation, completion rates, time-to-hire, research throughput. Shape a diagnostic that leads to a defined follow-on engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Conversion to implementation.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the transition from paid diagnostic to multi-line mandate, with a target of converting half of all audit engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proposals and bids.&lt;/strong&gt; Assemble proposals across the five service lines with the practice heads, price them against the finance model and qualify them against margin floors. Lead RFP and framework responses, including public-sector tenders in Germany and the UK.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder coverage.&lt;/strong&gt; Engage rectors, deans, CIOs, heads of digital learning, procurement, works councils, CLOs, HR directors and research directors. Maintain at least three engaged contacts on every opportunity above €200K.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner channel.&lt;/strong&gt; Recruit and manage regional partners, resellers, agencies and academic networks that extend reach beyond your direct coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quota and forecasting.&lt;/strong&gt; You carry an annual new-business quota, with quarterly KPIs covering pipeline coverage, audit conversion, average engagement value and blended margin. Maintain weekly pipeline hygiene in the CRM, submit a forecast you can defend, and flag slippage as soon as you see it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market feedback.&lt;/strong&gt; Report what EMEA buyers procure and what they decline, and how our pricing compares with Instructure, D2L, Cornerstone and the generalist integrators, so that the service catalogue can be adjusted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External representation.&lt;/strong&gt; Speak at sector events and contribute to thought leadership alongside our principal investigators, building recognition for CLS among education buyers in your region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Targets and KPIs&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role carries a quota set on net-new signed bookings (total contract value) in your territory, with a six-month ramp and a quarterly review:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Net-new signed bookings (TCV)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reference clients signed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Average engagement value&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit-to-implementation conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Blended gross margin on signed work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New qualified opportunities created&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forecast accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network in the sector.&lt;/strong&gt; Eight or more years selling into education, research or corporate learning in EMEA, preferably DACH and/or the UK, with decision-maker relationships you can open within the first 90 days. You should be prepared to discuss your top 15 target accounts and the route into each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A closing record in complex services.&lt;/strong&gt; Consistent achievement against a quota of €1M or more in professional services, consulting, systems integration or enterprise EdTech, covering six-figure deals, multi-stakeholder buying groups and six- to twelve-month cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consultative selling.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience selling scoped engagements whose deliverables were defined jointly with the client, and fluency in a recognized methodology such as MEDDIC, Challenger or Command of the Message.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain credibility.&lt;/strong&gt; The ability to hold a substantive conversation with a pro-vice-chancellor about digitalization, a CLO about competency frameworks or a research director about co-funded projects, together with a working understanding of how universities and research organizations buy: budget cycles, committee approval, procurement frameworks and public tender rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfort in an early-stage unit.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience building a territory or a new offering from a standing start, and the ability to sell a service catalogue that is still being completed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages.&lt;/strong&gt; Business-fluent &lt;strong&gt;German&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;English&lt;/strong&gt;. Both are required, since public education buyers in DACH contract in German.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial discipline.&lt;/strong&gt; Rigorous CRM and forecasting practice, and a readiness to qualify out early rather than carry unlikely deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional integrity.&lt;/strong&gt; You will represent a research institution to universities and public bodies, so commitments made during the sales process must be ones delivery can meet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling into publicly funded research programmes, or EU and national grant-co-funded projects (Horizon Europe, Innovate UK, BMBF).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the LMS/SIS landscape and its incumbents — Instructure, D2L, Cornerstone, Moodle, SAP SuccessFactors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UK public procurement frameworks (Crown Commercial Service, JISC) or German public tendering (VgV, e-Vergabe).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in the education practice of a systems integrator, Big Four firm or consultancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior success selling talent, recruitment or academic content services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French, Italian or Dutch as a third language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing speaking profile in the education or L&amp;amp;D community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location and travel&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates must be based in Europe and hold an existing, unrestricted right to work in their country of residence. &lt;strong&gt;Relocation is not offered for this position:&lt;/strong&gt; the network the role depends on should already be in the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred bases are Germany, Switzerland, Bulgaria or the UK. The role is remote or hybrid, with regular time in Bremen and at the London commercial hub. Expect travel of up to 40% within EMEA for client meetings, tenders and sector events, plus occasional travel to other Constructor locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we offer&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base salary and commission&lt;/strong&gt;, weighted approximately 60/40 at on-target earnings, with accelerators above 100% of quota. The band is competitive for a Director-level individual contributor in DACH or the UK and depends on location and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A guaranteed ramp&lt;/strong&gt; across the first two quarters while the pipeline is built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commission on margin as well as revenue&lt;/strong&gt;, so that well-scoped work is rewarded ahead of discounted work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access to our researchers&lt;/strong&gt;, including principal investigators, CERN-level data scientists, and education methodologists who will join your client meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An existing reference base&lt;/strong&gt;, including named proctoring and platform deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence over the offering.&lt;/strong&gt; As the key commercial voice in these markets, you will shape a service catalogue that is not yet fixed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin is the world’s leading platform for savings and investment products. Founded in 2012, the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech&lt;/strong&gt; connects consumers with banks in the EU, the UK and the US. This gives consumers &lt;strong&gt;better interest rates&lt;/strong&gt; and banks a &lt;strong&gt;diversified form of refinancing&lt;/strong&gt;. Our vision is to offer savings and investments without barriers and thus open up the global 160 trillion euro market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;sc-gEkIjz cjtSrT MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 sc-hoLEA&quot;&gt;Raisin currently employs more than 800 people from over 75 countries worldwide. Today, the platform holds over 80 billion euros in assets from&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;more than one million investors&lt;/strong&gt; which have accrued over 5 billion euros in returns.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For further development and expansion of our successful business, Raisin is looking for a highly motivated, driven, and experienced &lt;strong&gt;Director of Engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to lead both strategically and operationally our Investment and Pension (IPP) teams (25+ engineers)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces high-quality conceptual and delivery performance of the teams, the health of the IPP engineering organization and system landscape,&amp;nbsp; an efficient and compliant development process, technical and business ownership of the Raisin’s IPP platform, and vendor relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we work in a domain driven organization with a binary-star leadership model. In this model, every Director of Engineering has a Product partner (Head of Product/ Director of Product).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director Engineering (DE) leads both strategically and operationally across multiple cross-functional teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This embraces the six impact areas (in details below):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery quality and speed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;accountable for fulfilling the agreed team commitments to their business-owners in time, scope, and budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;responsible for the performance of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;resolving impediments for their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing a culture of accountability, pragmatism, and reusability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading both complex technical and important business projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leading internal software engineering projects and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;drives long-term value creation for their domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is fostering an environment of passion and fun for the business processes in their tribe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;builds resilient domain expertise in their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;has a deep understanding of the existing system landscape of their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;collaborates closely with their Business Owner and other stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;vendor management (evaluating, onboarding, and managing vendors)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;shapes the technical strategy for their teams according to the Raisin&#39;s business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;collaborates closely with other Sr. Engineering Leads in shaping and implementing Raisin&#39;s Tech Strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;actively initiates and contributes to strategic technical and architectural decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;is always considering the strategic benefits and price of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;keeping an existing technical solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;introducing a new alternative (e.g framework, tech stack, tooling, process)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;fully responsible for the health, resilience high performance, and development of their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;offering direct leadership of engineering leads and sometimes also tech leads as well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;encouraging accountability, creativity, risk-taking, and ownership by delegating responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;attracting, hiring, and retaining top technical talent for Raisin from around the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;proactively mentoring and coaching individual team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ensuring a strong delivery-oriented collaboration between the different engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;organizing workshops/hackathons&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;representing the company in external tech events advancing Raisin’s tech brand recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;shaping and driving knowledge transfer best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;nurturing and protecting our culture of trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;initiating, owning and nurturing tech initiatives (like guilds, workshops, regular meetups)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;recognizing high performance and rewarding accomplishments within their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process and Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The DE:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;drives, improves, and applies existing Raisin standards and policies, regulation and data privacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;contributes to an optimal toolchain with a high level of automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;develops, establishes, and continually improves documentation standards for the engineering organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;develops guidelines and best practices to ensure a lean software development process across different product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;is responsible for the KPI-based reporting for their teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;actively monitors, analyses, and drives initiatives to continuously reduce their teams&#39; technical debt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You hold a university degree in Computer Science,&amp;nbsp; Engineering, Information Systems, or related fields or have equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Leadership experience 10y+. You are a senior engineering leader, across projects and teams, with a natural aptitude and passion for growing and developing high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have at least 4y experience in FinTech&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain knowledge of Investment products is a strong advantage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong business mindset&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Strong AWS knowledge, Java, SQL, Kafka or other messaging solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are pragmatic and can handle the balance between both taking and delegating the lead in challenging situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You bring both strong strategic and excellent operational leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You motivate and inspire by outstanding communication and interpersonal skills, both written and verbal, including communicating technical concepts to non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You possess solid engineering background and distinct hands-on mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are experienced with OKR and KPI-based target agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are familiar with architecturally-heavy systems, including designing, implementing, and evolving these system constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;You are fluent in English, knowledge of German or another European language would be a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join our mission, join our team – and grow with us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Raisin, we care about each other and it is one of our top priorities to foster an open and caring environment in which everyone feels welcome and comfortable. Our culture is strongly driven by our ambitious team, which connects more than 75 different nationalities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will benefit from:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Development Budget of €2,000 and four full training days per year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours, home office and 30 vacation days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension scheme (Betriebliche Altersvorsorge), which we support with 20%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy more than 50+ different sports with Urban Sports Club: We subsidize your membership with more than €20 per month.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do you miss being in the office? The Deutschland Ticket gets you there, which we subsidize with €25 per month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love cycling? With JobRad, lease the bike of your choice and enjoy tax savings, plus Raisin covers your monthly insurance costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hungry all the time? Snacks, daily fresh fruit as well as drinks provided at the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are moving from another country or city to join us? We may support your relocation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.raisin.com/corporate/raisin-applicant-privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Raisin Applicant Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;728&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;We value diversity and the unique experiences each individual brings. If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;907&quot; data-end=&quot;1013&quot;&gt;We are an equal opportunity employer and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for everyone, regardless of race, colour, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, or gender identity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join Collibra’s Sales team as a Senior Account Executive, UKI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make an impact at Collibra by fueling our growth in your assigned territory of UKI and be the guiding force behind bringing Collibra&#39;s value and vision to customers and prospects. As part of our Enterprise Sales team, you will manage some of Collibra’s largest customers and prospects. In this role, you will use your knowledge in Enterprise SaaS sales to establish trusted and credible relationships, build Collibra’s brand and awareness around our solution, and serve as a Data Intelligence advisor throughout the customer journey, driving demand, adoption and expansion for Collibra solutions within your territory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our London office.&amp;nbsp;Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Account Executives are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospecting for net new accounts, greenfield building, and developing relationships with existing customers to maintain active deal pipeline and ideal quota coverage in your territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and create demand for expansion on existing customers to widen the footprint of Collibra within these accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing complex deal cycles, from lead origination to stakeholder mapping, through negotiation to close and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully collaborating with customers, partners, and peers in a consultative sales process where you will identify value and ROI to support customer’s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliable, accurate forecasting, with Salesforce updates reflective of real-time activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently achieved or overachieved your SaaS sales quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the Data Management domain highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Originated and navigated complex, direct sales cycles with multiple technical and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sold net-new business and expansion opportunities to C-level buyers in large enterprise accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed consultative sales processes, with value-based impacts or outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 2-3 years of experience in data management sales familiar with corresponding sales methodologies and comprehensible track records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent related working experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Known for your integrity, and commitment to the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Composed, resourceful, and focused in high-growth environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable traveling when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptive, accountable, and execution-oriented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A precise communicator and persuasive negotiator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proud of your work and aim for excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible to travel as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
